OL,3,GNEWSAReducing pothole-fixing machine
OL,4,Afleet 'a concern'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA fleet of pothole-fixing vehicles has
OL,7,Fbeen cut despite a council previously
OL,8,Fsaying the speed and efficiency of the
OL,9,Fmachines had been a "game changer".
OL,11,FThe leader of Wiltshire Council Ian
OL,12,FThorn said a fleet of three bobcat
OL,13,Fmachines were reduced to two in July
OL,14,Fgiving it "greater flexibility to
OL,15,Finvest in a range of highway
OL,16,Fmaintenance activities".
OL,18,FHowever, some councillors including
OL,19,FDominic Muns, said the decision was "a
OL,20,Fconcern", questioning whether the
OL,21,Fcouncil had genuinely caught up with
OL,22,Fits backlog of pothole repairs.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,350,340,200,160,0,100
